o=A.u4(A.b(["Step 1: Register through State Horticulture/Agriculture Department portal.","Step 2: Select registered micro-irrigation manufacturer/vendor.","Step 3: Field verification and GPS survey by horticulture officer.","Step 4: Installation followed by subsidy transfer to bank or vendor."],f),d,h,"Focuses on enhancing water use efficiency at farm level through precision micro-irrigation, moisture conservation, and farm ponds to achieve Har Khet Ko Pani and More Crop Per Drop.",e,"scheme_pmksy",i,"PM Krishi Sinchayee Yojana (Per Drop More Crop)","Ministry of Jal Shakti & Dept of Agriculture","https://pmksy.gov.in",o,"Up to 55% subsidy on micro-irrigation systems (Drip and Sprinkler) to maximize water use efficiency.")
e=A.b(["All farmers across India possessing agricultural land."],f)
d=A.b(["Detailed status report on 12 parameters: N, P, K, S, Zn, Fe, Cu, Mn, Bo, pH, EC, and OC.","Dosage advisory for specific crops to reduce wasteful fertilizer expenditure by 15-20%.","Guidance on soil amendments like gypsum or lime for alkaline/acidic soils."],f)
n=A.b(["Aadhaar Card","Land identification survey number","Mobile number for digital SMS delivery"],f)
n=A.u4(A.b(["Step 1: Soil samples collected by agricultural department field workers.","Step 2: Samples tested in designated district Soil Testing Laboratories (STLs).","Step 3: Soil Health Card generated and printed or downloaded via soilhealth.dac.gov.in."],f),d,g,"Assists farmers in improving productivity through judicious use of chemical fertilizers, organic compost, and micro-nutrients based on periodic laboratory soil analysis.",e,"scheme_soil_health","December 2024","Soil Health Card (SHC) Scheme","Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare","https://soilhealth.dac.gov.in",n,"Free soil testing and customized nutrient recommendations issued every 2 years.")
